course: dictionary
lesson: 4956
title: Big words for big occasions
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An inauguration is a formal ceremony, a special public event with set rules. It has two meanings. In the first, it brings a new leader into office. In the second, it is the official opening or start of something new. «A new president's term starts on Inauguration Day, 20 January, with an oath to "preserve, protect and defend" the Constitution.» The words term, oath and Day are clues: this is a serious occasion where someone makes a solemn promise to start a job.
explain: Read the words around it, then test your meaning in the sentence. «In 2025 it was reported the ceremony was moved indoors because of the cold.» The word ceremony is a clue: an inauguration is a ceremony. Try swapping in your meaning: "the new leader's start to office was moved indoors because of the cold." It still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Decide which meaning fits by looking at what is being started. A leader in the sentence means meaning one. A new bridge, school or building means meaning two. The phrase inaugural speech is a clue too: an inaugural speech is the first speech given at a start, such as a new leader's first speech.
fact: An inauguration is a formal ceremony to bring a new leader into office.
fact: An inauguration is also the official opening or start of something new, like a building or a festival.
fact: «Inauguration Day» is 20 January in the US, when a new president's term starts.
fact: The new president takes an oath, which is a serious promise, to preserve, protect and defend the Constitution.
fact: Useful phrases: inauguration day, inaugural speech, inauguration ceremony.
exercise: «A new president's term starts on Inauguration Day, 20 January.» What is an inauguration? | *A formal ceremony that brings a new leader into office | A kind of rain storm | A holiday for shopping and sales
exercise: The town held an ___ for its new bridge, with a big ribbon cutting. Which word fits best? | argument | holiday | *inauguration | sleepover
exercise: Find and copy the word in «the ceremony was moved indoors because of the cold» that means a formal event. | moved | *ceremony | indoors | cold
test: The school held an inauguration for its new library. Which meaning fits here? | A new leader being elected by the children | *The official opening of something new | A type of school lunch
test: Why does an oath matter in an inauguration? | *It shows the leader promises to do the job well | It stops the ceremony from starting | It is a kind of song everyone must sing
exam: Which sentence uses inauguration correctly? | The dog had an inauguration of fleas. | *The inauguration of the new swimming pool was attended by the mayor. | We ate an inauguration for lunch.
